cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Season-dependent drought accumulation scales for cropland monitoring and yield
  modelling in rainfed Turkish Thrace — code and derived data
message: >-
  If you use this software or the derived data, please cite both the archive and
  the accompanying article.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kıvrak
    given-names: Cantekin
    affiliation: >-
      Atatürk Soil, Water and Agricultural Meteorology Research Institute,
      Kırklareli, Türkiye
    email: cantekin.kivrak@tarimorman.gov.tr
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6221-2469'
  - family-names: Şener
    given-names: Mehmet
    affiliation: 'Namık Kemal University, Biosystems Engineering, Tekirdağ, Türkiye'
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6736-0567'
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived, analysis-ready data reproducing the scale-selection,
  seasonal-window, compositing-sensitivity, robustness, yield-modelling and
  spatial-aggregation results of the accompanying article (revised version).
  A cropland Landsat Vegetation Health Index (30 m, CORINE class 211 mask, monthly
  median composite, alpha = 0.5) is evaluated against SPI and SPEI at five
  accumulation scales over seven districts of Turkish Thrace, 1985-2024; the
  per-scene district table from which every compositing and mask variant can be
  rebuilt is included.
keywords:
  - agricultural drought
  - SPEI
  - Landsat
  - Vegetation Health Index
  - time-scale selection
  - seasonal windows
  - compositing
  - sunflower yield
  - Turkish Thrace
